  "title": "Supplementary Table S23. Attrition sensitivity analyses.",
  "panel": "B",
  "panel_title": "Panel b. Joint-model contrasts under inverse-probability-of-attrition weighting (N = 5,938 observations).",
  "notes_before": [],
  "notes_after": [
    "Note. Joint mixed-effects models with participant-level random intercepts, fitted with combined inverse-probability-of-attrition and exposure weights (winsorised at the 1st/99th percentiles; retained-participant mean attrition weight 1.54, range 1.31–2.00). Reference group: low EVI/low O₃. The difference-in-differences interaction estimates departure from additivity of mean BAA differences. Of 3,197 baseline participants, 2,972 could be scored by the retention model (model frame 4,587 of 4,954 eligible participants)."
  ],
